<PublicLayout.public>
  <section class="ck-shell ck-shell-tight">
    <div class="ck-section-header">
      <div>
        <p class="ck-kicker">Getting started</p>
        <h1 class="ck-section-title">Install to first finding in five minutes</h1>
        <p class="ck-lead ck-lead-tight">
          ControlKeel turns project rules, domain knowledge, and security boundaries into findings, proofs, approval gates, budgets, evals, and durable context across supported hosts. Agent output is cheap; reviewability, release safety, and cost control are not. ControlKeel governs that loop from the first attach.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ck-shell ck-shell-tight" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <p class="ck-mini-label">Install</p>
      <%= for channel <- @install_channels do %>
        <article
          class="rounded-3xl border border-white/10 bg-zinc-950/70 p-5 transition hover:border-lime-300/40 hover:bg-zinc-950/90"
          id={"install-channel-#{channel.id}"}
        >
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:items-start sm:justify-between">
            <div class="space-y-3">
              <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
                <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white">{channel.label}</h3>
                <span class="rounded-full bg-white/5 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-zinc-300">
                  {Enum.join(channel.platforms, ", ")}
                </span>
              </div>
              <p class="text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-400">{channel.description}</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-black/10">
            <pre class="whitespace-pre-wrap px-4 py-3 text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-100"><code>{channel.command}</code></pre>
          </div>
        </article>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <.available_where agent_integrations={@agent_integrations} />
  </section>

  <section class="ck-shell ck-shell-tight" style="padding-top:0">
    <p class="ck-mini-label">Quick start</p>
    <div class="ck-grid mt-4">
      <div class="ck-card">
        <p class="ck-mini-label">Packaged binary</p>
        <ol class="ck-mini-list mt-4">
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            1. Run
            <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-200">controlkeel</code>
            to boot the local web app.
          </li>
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            2. In your project, run <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-200">controlkeel setup</code>, then <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-200">controlkeel attach opencode</code>.
          </li>
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            3. Binding auto-bootstraps on first use; use
            <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-200">
              controlkeel bootstrap
            </code>
            or
            <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-200">controlkeel init</code>
            to do it explicitly.
          </li>
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            4. Run <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-200">controlkeel attach doctor</code>, <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-200">controlkeel provider doctor</code>, and <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-200">controlkeel status</code>.
          </li>
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            5. Trigger a controlled validation, then open Mission Control or run
            <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-200">
              controlkeel findings
            </code>
            to verify the block.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="ck-card">
        <p class="ck-mini-label">Source setup</p>
        <ol class="ck-mini-list mt-4">
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            1. Run <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-200">mix setup</code>
            once.
          </li>
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            2. Run
            <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-200">mix phx.server</code>
            in the ControlKeel repo.
          </li>
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            3. In your project, run
            <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-200">
              mix ck.attach opencode
            </code>
            from the same source environment.
          </li>
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            4. <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-200">mix ck.init</code>
            is available for explicit setup.
          </li>
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            5. Run a built-in smoke benchmark or validate a pending change to trigger the first finding.
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="ck-note mt-4 text-sm">
      Attach defaults to project scope and writes inside the governed repository. User scope is available only for hosts that advertise it. Local stdio MCP exposes the full local tool set; hosted MCP is a separate, narrower OAuth-scoped surface.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="ck-shell ck-shell-tight" style="padding-top:0">
    <p class="ck-mini-label">How it governs</p>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 mt-4">
      <div class="ck-card">
        <p class="ck-mini-label">Governed delivery lifecycle</p>
        <ul class="ck-mini-list mt-3">
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            Intent intake and execution briefs at
            <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-200">/missions/start</code>
          </li>
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            Task graph, validation, and findings during execution
          </li>
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            Proof bundles, Ship Dashboard, and benchmarks as evidence
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="ck-card">
        <p class="ck-mini-label">Proof console loop</p>
        <ul class="ck-mini-list mt-3">
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            Mission Control for active task state, risk, and approvals
          </li>
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            Findings turn policy violations into reviewable work
          </li>
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            Proof Browser for immutable evidence and rollback guidance
          </li>
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            Ship Dashboard and benchmarks for outcome evidence
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="ck-card">
        <p class="ck-mini-label">Autonomy and findings</p>
        <p class="ck-note mt-3 text-sm">
          Severity maps to expected human gates; findings stay readable in plain language. LLM advisory is optional and needs a provider. See <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-200">docs/autonomy-and-findings.md</code>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="ck-card">
        <p class="ck-mini-label">Operating modes</p>
        <ul class="ck-mini-list mt-3">
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            Local mode ships with SQLite, Ollama, or heuristic fallback.
          </li>
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            Cloud mode connects orgs, projects, users, webhooks, and service accounts as shared governance evidence.
          </li>
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            Use benchmarks to collect bounded evidence before claiming a workflow is safer, cheaper, or faster.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="ck-card">
        <p class="ck-mini-label">Occupation-first onboarding</p>
        <p class="ck-note mt-3 text-sm">
          Start from what best describes your work. ControlKeel picks the domain pack, interview language, and governance posture behind the scenes, so non-experts don't need to choose a framework first.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="ck-card">
        <p class="ck-mini-label">Project rescue</p>
        <p class="ck-note mt-3 text-sm">
          If another tool already touched the repo, bootstrap it, run <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-200">controlkeel watch</code>, and use findings, proofs, and
          <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-200">ck_validate</code>
          to recover. Add governed proxy only when the tool points at compatible OpenAI or Anthropic endpoints.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ck-shell ck-shell-tight" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="ck-grid">
      <div class="ck-card">
        <p class="ck-mini-label">Other supported agents</p>
        <ul class="ck-mini-list mt-3">
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-200">
              controlkeel attach codex-cli
            </code>
            installs native Codex skills and the CK operator agent.
          </li>
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-200">
              controlkeel attach vscode
            </code>
            and
            <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1.5 py-0.5 text-zinc-200">
              controlkeel attach copilot
            </code>
            prepare repo-native skills plus MCP config.
          </li>
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
            OpenCode is the recommended quick start; Cursor, Windsurf, Kiro, Amp, Gemini CLI, Continue, and Aider use the same portable bundle path.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <a href="https://github.com/aryaminus/controlkeel" class="ck-link mt-4 inline-block">
          Learn more on GitHub
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="ck-card">
        <p class="ck-mini-label">What it is not</p>
        <ul class="ck-mini-list mt-3">
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">Not another IDE or coding model</li>
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">Not a prompt marketplace or generic memory API</li>
          <li class="text-sm text-zinc-400">Not passive monitoring or post-hoc review only</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</PublicLayout.public>
